# ripple_block_end

- Label: Ripple Block End
- Category: Copernicus (`Cop`), Houdini 22.0.368
- Inputs: 0 to 2
- Parameters: 18 (exact, read from Houdini by hython)
- Used by the height graph: no

## Feature summary (web, SideFX reference)

- Source: https://www.sidefx.com/docs/houdini/nodes/cop/ripple_block_end.html
- Summary (EN): Ripple Block End marks the end of a Ripple simulation block in Copernicus and must be paired with a Ripple Block Begin. When Simulate is on, its outputs feed back into its inputs, creating the simulation loop.
- Résumé (FR) : Le nœud Ripple Block End referme un bloc de simulation de vagues et renvoie ses résultats dans la boucle quand Simulate est activé.

- Inputs meaning: ["height: the wave height", "feedback: cable of the current feedback data routed back into the input; its structure must match the initial structure set on the Block Begin"]

- Key parameters: ["Simulate: turns on the feedback loop", "Reset Simulation: clears the whole simulation cache when Simulate is on", "Time Scale: scales time inside the block; above 1 speeds up, below 1 slows down", "Substeps: divides each frame into this many substeps, for accuracy and stability with fast ripples", "Iterations: number of iterations when not simulating", "Live Simulation: interactive, non-deterministic mode independent of the playbar, not cached", "Caching, Start Frame, Cached Frames, Checkpoint Rate: frame caching controls", "Wave Speed: how fast ripples travel across pixels", "Conservation: how much wave velocity is kept over time; 1 keeps all velocity, values outside 0 to 1 are clamped", "Spring: strength of the force pulling pixels back toward rest (called Rest Spring in the introduction)"]

- Caveats: ["Requires DOP-level permissions: not in Houdini Core, only in Houdini FX, Apprentice, Indie and Education", "Compiled COP networks do not support simulation", "Live Simulation does not save results; use a Stash COP to keep them", "When Live Simulation is on, Start Frame, Cached Frames and Checkpoint Rate no longer apply"]

